{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1339 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "084477bf58771515909dd9a7888d66bcaa4c4dde4300e449ab82e7fedf5bf7f8" :edb/db-before-t 1338 :edb/db-after-t 1339 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534651 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:15:38.516Z" 13194139534651 true] [17592186157238 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301496 13194139534651 true] [17592186157238 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301503 13194139534651 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301478 13194139534651 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301485 13194139534651 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301491 13194139534651 true] [17592186301478 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301479 13194139534651 true] [17592186301478 1089 "q-106500" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301478 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534651 true] [17592186301478 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx+3=4t,\\,y+5=2{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301478 1113 #uuid "25eb3505-f2cc-55ce-9408-26205e80e549" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301478 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\frac{x+3}{4},\\,{t}^{2}=\\frac{y+5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{x+3}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{y+5}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{y+5}{2} \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =8(y+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301480 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301481 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301482 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301483 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301484 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1041 "selection" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301480 13194139534651 true] [17592186301479 1110 #uuid "89c55efa-1538-525f-bb1c-75d79c3dc25e" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301480 1034 "(x+3)^{2}=8(y+5)" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301480 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301480 1111 #uuid "7d075df6-453f-5ecc-ad12-d83d346032df" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301481 1034 "(x-3)^{2}=8(y+5)" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301481 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301481 1111 #uuid "3b1e0cae-033a-58f1-bc21-33616af1195b" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301482 1034 "(x+3)^{2}=4(y+5)" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301482 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301482 1111 #uuid "d96474cc-e09a-5429-9d2e-8594f2e6a3d3" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301483 1034 "(x-3)^{2}=8(y-5)" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301483 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301483 1111 #uuid "a6f2c6c2-2963-59fb-bb96-05c32b2ce4a5" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301484 1034 "(x+5)^{2}=8(y+3)" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301484 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301484 1111 #uuid "ba47b123-29fb-5295-86c2-cdd0ead646d9" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301485 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301486 13194139534651 true] [17592186301485 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301489 13194139534651 true] [17592186301485 1089 "q-323221" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301485 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534651 true] [17592186301485 1100 "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola \n\n$$\nx+2=4{t}^{2},\\,y-1=8t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(y\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534651 true] [17592186301485 1113 #uuid "41d94804-48b6-5be3-bce5-5a3693e0aa7f" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301485 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x+2}{4},\\,t=\\frac{y-1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{y-1}{8})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{x+2}{4}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{64} & =\\frac{x+2}{4} \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =64\\cdot (\\frac{x+2}{4}) \\\\ {(y-1)}^{2} & =16(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301486 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301487 13194139534651 true] [17592186301486 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301488 13194139534651 true] [17592186301486 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534651 true] [17592186301486 1041 "field-1" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301486 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301488 13194139534651 true] [17592186301486 1110 #uuid "3061b774-768d-5945-a930-8745bdd46602" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301487 1034 "2" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301487 1111 #uuid "2cadca9a-952d-5491-b921-3a5909d67b8f" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301488 1034 "1" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301488 1111 #uuid "7953bd5c-fdb5-54b4-a64a-f33c99953715" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301489 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301490 13194139534651 true] [17592186301489 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534651 true] [17592186301489 1041 "field-2" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301489 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301490 13194139534651 true] [17592186301489 1110 #uuid "ad12e0ad-90cf-5c2c-9566-a9e11b32e5ca" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301490 1034 "16(x+2)" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301490 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301490 1111 #uuid "460fda13-8ff8-575a-a3cf-2b8ef5ddcc18" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301491 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301492 13194139534651 true] [17592186301491 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301494 13194139534651 true] [17592186301491 1089 "q-323230" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301491 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534651 true] [17592186301491 1100 "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola \n\n$$\nx+1=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,y-2=-t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(y\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534651 true] [17592186301491 1113 #uuid "0253ece9-d579-587e-a8e2-8a9065f5b162" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301491 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =-4(x+1),\\,t=-(y-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-(y-2))}^{2} \\\\  & =(y-2)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-4(x+1)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =-4(x+1) \\\\ {(y-2)}^{2} & =-4(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301492 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301493 13194139534651 true] [17592186301492 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534651 true] [17592186301492 1041 "field-1" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301492 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301493 13194139534651 true] [17592186301492 1110 #uuid "49218b6d-88c5-533f-be7a-01f0a13802c1" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301493 1034 "2" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301493 1111 #uuid "5fcd0123-fbe8-574b-ab52-e1ad3647585d" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301494 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301495 13194139534651 true] [17592186301494 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534651 true] [17592186301494 1041 "field-2" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301494 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301495 13194139534651 true] [17592186301494 1110 #uuid "28a2e027-ce5e-567b-ab57-514ff72fe68c" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301495 1034 "-4(x+1)" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301495 1111 #uuid "4b9925a6-9f06-5ca1-b8d7-af5197d5cb66" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301496 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301497 13194139534651 true] [17592186301496 1089 "q-84840" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301496 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534651 true] [17592186301496 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039044/assets/0d278fe1bf34cd60877be6886c90e1734fab7433f9f94ad7765d379e69c2da42.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301496 1113 #uuid "84bc7a7c-9e6f-5cc0-a103-68903527aa4c" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301496 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(2,2),$ and passes through the point $(4,6).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(2,2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-2=p{t}^{2},\\,y-2=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(4,6),$ we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=6$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 4=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-2=(2){t}^{2},\\,y-2=2(2)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-2=2{t}^{2},\\,y-2=4t.\n$$" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301498 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301499 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301500 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301501 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301502 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1041 "selection" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301499 13194139534651 true] [17592186301497 1110 #uuid "6baca86a-7538-54f8-b930-9937030a4c0e" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301498 1034 "x-2=2{t}^{2},\\,y-2=2t" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301498 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301498 1111 #uuid "d1e627b7-bfd6-534e-830d-90b90bf24d0f" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301499 1034 "x-2=2{t}^{2},\\,y-2=4t" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301499 1111 #uuid "6598d4bd-0f51-59f8-96b1-480f3601275c" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301500 1034 "x+2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+2=t" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301500 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301500 1111 #uuid "809636ff-d992-572c-a491-dbcaab56b899" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301501 1034 "x-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y-2=t" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301501 1111 #uuid "36b5d164-c361-542e-8465-94bac038821d" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301502 1034 "x+2=2{t}^{2},\\,y+2=4t" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301502 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534651 true] [17592186301502 1111 #uuid "96e52685-a506-5142-9b93-9931257df6a3" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301503 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301504 13194139534651 true] [17592186301503 1089 "q-84843" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301503 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534651 true] [17592186301503 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039044/assets/ba3d2c8719c97911d2339548f08601b07bcfe555d59dbb058a157836c45a34fe.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301503 1113 #uuid "23c1a911-6224-553e-84b2-80970be0d8e0" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301503 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(-4,2),$ and passes through the point $(-5,4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-4,2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+4=p{t}^{2},\\,y-2=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-5,4),$ we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=4$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-1=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 2=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2pt \\\\ 1 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =p{(\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -1 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+4=(-1){t}^{2},\\,y-2=2(-1)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+4=-{t}^{2},\\,y-2=-2t.\n$$" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301505 13194139534651 true] [17592186301504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301506 13194139534651 true] [17592186301504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301507 13194139534651 true] [17592186301504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301508 13194139534651 true] [17592186301504 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301509 13194139534651 true] [17592186301504 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534651 true] [17592186301504 1041 "selection" 13194139534651 true] [17592186301504 1104